{"kind":"assert","text":"Operating note: the inguz.space sandbox zone, for planner and builder. Follows the S0 addition in clarification f89c614b.\n\nPurpose. inguz.space is dap's sandbox origin domain for MCP Apps screens, the counterpart of the chat hosts' own content domains. A card runs on \u003cid\u003e.inguz.space, a registrable domain separate from every dap page, so a screen can never read a member page's keys, cookies or storage. The only channel between a screen and its host is JSON-RPC over postMessage. Nothing on this zone ever sets a cookie or holds a credential.\n\nState on 2026-10-17 23:25 UTC.\n- Zone inguz.space, id 409097ad75d6467e195559baea3ea663, type full, on the Cloudflare account \"inguz ᛜ outcomes\" (6e953d231f1c9aadffbf59537a82e13a), the same account as artroom-scope, artroom-rehearsal, artroom-jam and the other artroom Workers. Active since 23:24 UTC. Nameservers katja.ns.cloudflare.com and plato.ns.cloudflare.com; the registrar is domain.com, which Hugh manages.\n- DNS: proxied AAAA 100:: on the apex (record bae12a7e3985c92ccfc90503d6f344c6) and on *.inguz.space (record 40b6ec7b1597baef76210e5045e54770). They are Workers-route placeholders and serve nothing by themselves.\n- Settings: SSL strict, always-use-HTTPS on, minimum TLS 1.2. Universal SSL is enabled; the certificate pack was not yet issued at 23:25 and issues on its own. Check with: cf ssl certificate-packs list -z inguz.space.\n- Hostnames stay one label deep. The universal certificate covers inguz.space and *.inguz.space only; a.b.inguz.space would fail TLS.\n\nHow to deploy the sandbox shim.\n- One Worker on the same account, deployed with the same credentials and wrangler flow as the existing artroom Workers. Routes in its wrangler config: pattern \"*.inguz.space/*\" with zone_name \"inguz.space\", and \"inguz.space/*\" for the apex if it should answer. If the deploy refuses the route, the token lacks Workers Routes edit on this zone; mint one with cf accounts tokens create (see the cf CLI notes in the planner's memory).\n- The shim serves only the static sandbox proxy page. It receives the screen's HTML from the host over postMessage, writes it into an inner frame, sets the content security policy from the resource's _meta.ui.csp (connect, resource, frame and base-URI domains) and the frame allow list from _meta.ui.permissions, and relays JSON-RPC both ways. The reference host in the ext-apps repository (examples/basic-host) is the model; the specification reserves ui/notifications/sandbox-proxy-ready and ui/notifications/sandbox-resource-ready for this exchange.\n- The \u003cid\u003e label is derived from the package: its declared _meta.ui.domain when it names one, otherwise the presentation id digest, so that each application gets its own origin and a new presentation gets a new one unless it asks for a stable domain.\n- S2's views/hosts.ts sets _meta.ui.domain to the application's \u003cid\u003e.inguz.space value. Chat hosts derive their own sandbox hostnames from it; dap's own page, when it becomes a host, uses it directly.\n\nOperating the zone. cf dns records list -z inguz.space; cf zones settings get \u003csetting\u003e -z inguz.space; cf zones settings edit \u003csetting\u003e -z inguz.space --body '{\"value\":...}'. The cf CLI on Hugh's machine is logged in to this account. Rollback is deleting the two records; the domain has no other use.\n\nOut of scope for S0: the dap web host that would embed these screens on dap's own pages. That is a later request after the journey's exit test."}